# config.env.example
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPRECATED: config.env is no longer used by this overlay.
#
# Previously, infrastructure values from Terraform were written to config.env locally
# and read by Kustomize's configMapGenerator. This broke ArgoCD because config.env
# was gitignored and ArgoCD only has access to git-tracked files.
#
# The values are now stored in two places:
#
#   1. eso-config.yaml (committed to git)
#      A static ConfigMap manifest read by Kustomize replacements.
#      Safe to commit — these are infrastructure coordinates, not credentials.
#      Update this file when infrastructure changes (new Key Vault, new tenant, etc.).
#
#   2. ConfigMap on the cluster (provisioned by Terraform)
#      Created by providers/azure/modules/external_secrets/main.tf using
#      terraform_data.eso_config_secret. Stays in sync with Terraform state.
#      Re-run `terraform apply` after infrastructure changes.
#
# Keys that were previously in config.env:
#
#   TENANT_ID               — data.azurerm_client_config.current.tenant_id
#   KEY_VAULT_URI           — module.key_vault.key_vault_uri
#   SERVICE_ACCOUNT_NAME    — var.external_secrets_service_account
#   ESO_NAMESPACE           — var.external_secrets_namespace
#   CREDENTIALS_SECRET_NAME — var.credentials_secret_name
#   STOCK_TRADER_NAMESPACE  — var.stock_trader_namespace
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
